# Development Workflow

## Purpose

Codegen, local compose stack, benchmarks, fault injection runbooks, and admin release checks. Sources-only repo: run `make gen` / `make proto` after clone.

Requirements: Go 1.25+, Docker Compose, `make`, clang/llvm for eBPF, Linux 5.8+ (XDP 6.1+).

## Codegen

```bash
make gen # sqlc -> internal/<svc>/db/*.sql.go
make proto # buf + patch-vtproto-hotpath
make gen bpf-dev # BPF -> internal/edge/bpf_edge_bpf*.go
```

Scaffold new service:

```bash
task scaffold -- my-service
task gen
task test-gen -- internal/my-service
```

ClickHouse canonical DDL: `internal/clickhouse/migrate/00000_bootstrap_tables.sql` must match `deploy/clickhouse/init.sql`.

## Local stack

Operator-owned. **Agents:** do not run `stack.sh up`, `docker compose up`, `prepare_test.sh`, or loop `go build`/`go test`/`typecheck` unless the operator explicitly requests it in the current turn (`anti-slop.mdc` **Compile and test ritual ban**, **Agent local environment**). Stopping: `bash scripts/dev/stack.sh down`.

```bash
cp .env.example .env
bash scripts/dev/stack.sh build
bash scripts/dev/stack.sh ingest-only
bash scripts/dev/preflight.sh
```

| Profile | Services |
| :--- | :--- |
| `ingest-only` (default dev) | tracker, processor, control, PG, Redis; **no CH** |
| `single-vps` / `full` | `REDIS_SHARD_COUNT` redis shards (local default 2); **CH not started** |
| `stack.sh clickhouse` | ClickHouse only; explicit opt-in |
| `infra` | PG, Redis x`REDIS_SHARD_COUNT` (max 6); **no CH** |
| `analytics-ml` | + fraud-scorer, ivt-detector, **CH required** |

### Redis shard count (dev)

`REDIS_SHARD_COUNT` in `.env` controls which `redis-0..redis-5` services `stack.sh` starts (max 6). `REDIS_ADDRS` must list one address per shard (`bash scripts/ops/verify_redis_topology.sh .env`).

| Variable | Default (local) | Role |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `REDIS_SHARD_COUNT` | 2 | Compose shard count |
| `INGEST_REDIS_SHARD_COUNT` | 2 | `ingest-only` starts `redis-0` and `redis-1` |
| `COMPOSE_MEMORY_PROFILE` | `dev` | Applies `docker-compose.memory-dev.yaml` cgroup limits |

Local default: 2 shards in `.env.example`. Production (`ENV=production`) still requires exactly `ExpectedRedisShardCount` (4) entries in `REDIS_ADDRS`.

### Docker memory (laptop)

`COMPOSE_MEMORY_PROFILE=dev` (default when unset in `stack.sh`) adds reduced cgroup limits. Set `COMPOSE_MEMORY_PROFILE=` in `.env` to use compose file defaults. ClickHouse overlay when started: ~1.5G limit in memory-dev profile.

### ClickHouse on dev laptops (critical)

Do **not** start ClickHouse for routine work. CH pulls ~4G compose limit, heavy disk I/O, and triggers OOM on 16GB hosts.

| Allowed | Command |
| :--- | :--- |
| Hotfix proving CH ingest / reports | `CH_ENABLED=1 bash scripts/dev/stack.sh clickhouse` then reproduce |
| P0 e2e needing analytics tables | same + targeted test; tear down after |
| IOPS / load-test BPF tier | `deploy/compose/docker-compose.load-test.yaml` on dedicated runner |

Forbidden without operator ask: `stack.sh full`, `infra`, `single-vps` with CH; `make test-integration` that needs CH while CH container runs for unrelated work; leaving `clickhouse` up overnight.

Default: `CH_ENABLED=0` in `.env.example` and compose. Processor/control skip CH when disabled (`internal/doctor` skips CH probe).

```bash
bash scripts/dev/stack.sh ingest-only   # canonical laptop path
```

Admin static (UI rebuild; `web/` absent):

```bash
go test ./internal/controlplane/ -run TestAdminStaticRoutes -count=1
bash scripts/ci/admin_web.sh
```

After milestone `admin_shell` (`web/dist` exists):

```bash
cd web && npm ci && npm run build
```

Bootstrap admin: `scripts/dev/seed_admin.sh`. E2E: `scripts/test/admin_stack_e2e.sh` (requires `web/` + e2e tree).

## Fault injection

Full matrix: `fault-tests.mdc`. Parser chaos: `parser.mdc`.

```bash
bash scripts/fault/run.sh
bash scripts/fault/compose_fault_drill.sh all
go test -run 'TestFault_' ./internal/ingestion/ ./internal/controlplane/
```

Success logs `fault_proof fault=<name>`.

## Broker cutover (`CH_INGEST_SOURCE=broker`)

Dual-path shadow (`BROKER_SHADOW_MODE=1`), drain PEL, then flip. Default appliance: broker-primary for CH ingest; Redis streams remain for budget Lua and `ad:fraud:stream`.

## Admin release (pre-tag)

While `web/` absent:

```bash
go test ./internal/controlplane/ -run TestAdminStaticRoutes -count=1
bash scripts/ci/admin_web.sh
bash scripts/ci/openapi_gate.sh
```

After `admin_shell`:

```bash
cd web && npm ci && npm run build && cd ..
go test ./internal/controlplane/ -run TestAdminStaticRoutes -count=1
bash scripts/ci/admin_web.sh
bash scripts/ci/admin_ui_release_gate.sh
```

## Pre-PR verification

```bash
bash scripts/ci/lint_gate.sh
bash scripts/ci/pr_fast.sh
```

